# Cite the software. The JOSS DOI and a `preferred-citation` block for the paper
# go in on acceptance.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this viewer in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "OcuLayer: a zero-install browser viewer for segmented ocular micro-tomography"
abstract: >-
  A zero-install browser viewer for segmented ocular micro-computed-tomography.
  Two linked 3D panes show a reference eye and the segmented tissue layers of a
  scan, with per-structure visibility, tri-planar slicing with solid caps, and
  camera synchronisation; a user's own meshes or manifest can be dropped onto
  the page and rendered beside the bundled data. The rendering core is a
  DOM-free ES module library that also runs headless under Node.
type: software
